From: Elian Doran <doran.adoris.elian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: anx7688: no data role change without a role switch

The PinePhone's DT links no USB role switch to the bridge (the port stays
peripheral), so role_sw is NULL: usb_role_switch_get_role() reads
USB_ROLE_NONE, never the role the bridge reports, and the status check that
runs every second while connected requested the change again each time,
logging "DATA role change requested to UFP" (the driver defines DEBUG) while
usb_role_switch_set_role() did nothing. Skip it without a role switch.

---
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/anx7688.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/anx7688.c
@@ -1134,7 +1134,12 @@
 	anx7688->data_role = dr_dfp ? TYPEC_HOST : TYPEC_DEVICE;
 	typec_set_data_role(anx7688->port, anx7688->data_role);
 
-	if (usb_role_switch_get_role(anx7688->role_sw) !=
+	/*
+	 * Without a role switch (the PinePhone's DT links none) its role reads
+	 * as none: the change would be requested, and logged, every second.
+	 */
+	if (anx7688->role_sw &&
+	    usb_role_switch_get_role(anx7688->role_sw) !=
 	    (dr_dfp ? USB_ROLE_HOST : USB_ROLE_DEVICE)) {
 		dev_dbg(anx7688->dev, "DATA role change requested to %s\n",
 			dr_dfp ? "DFP" : "UFP");
